WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.529 --> 00:00:03.621
(upbeat music)

00:00:03.621 --> 00:00:05.958
- [Narrator] Deep in the
heart of the Andes Mountains,

00:00:05.958 --> 00:00:10.125
one man is growing lots and
lots and lots of potatoes.

00:00:52.238 --> 00:00:54.348
Potatoes originated along the southern

00:00:54.348 --> 00:00:57.597
border of Peru close to 8,000 years ago.

00:00:57.597 --> 00:01:00.836
Julio lives near where
potato growth first thrived,

00:01:00.836 --> 00:01:05.003
in one of the most remote
locations in the country.

00:01:19.608 --> 00:01:22.705
Julio's family has lived in
the region for generations,

00:01:22.705 --> 00:01:25.554
and, thanks to the land's micro-climate,

00:01:25.554 --> 00:01:28.139
he's able to grow his unique
potatoes in high quantities.

00:01:28.139 --> 00:01:31.529
Julio is always experimenting
with new farming techniques

00:01:31.529 --> 00:01:33.775
and relies on other native potato farmers

00:01:33.775 --> 00:01:35.942
to create his new strains.

00:01:48.567 --> 00:01:51.150
(mellow music)

00:02:18.146 --> 00:02:20.907
Potatoes are not only a
staple in Julio's diet,

00:02:20.907 --> 00:02:23.421
they are the backbone of Peruvian cuisine,

00:02:23.421 --> 00:02:25.346
which is why Julio wants to push

00:02:25.346 --> 00:02:27.062
the boundaries of potato farming

00:02:27.062 --> 00:02:29.812
and continue his family's legacy.

